& [UserTarget]
  + get Cantor set up to run from SOP
  + Cantor does its own work from that SOP-launched agent process
  + Cantor performs updates as part of that work
  + Cantor generates its own succeeding SOP from there

& [Continuity]
  + this target extends the preserved nested Cantor LLM-host vision rather than replacing it
  + a slim outer Cantor may remain the launch and governance substrate for a larger inner Cantor and model
  + the product target is a continuing agent process and work cycle, not only a one-shot model experiment

& [RequiredDistinctions]
  + boot SOP identity is distinct from agent session identity
  + work objective selection planning execution verification and completion are distinct stages
  + read authority workspace mutation authority commit authority push authority provider authority and external-effect authority are distinct
  + a self-generated SOP is an attributable source or proposal until the applicable review and satisfaction-signature gates admit it
  + performing an update does not automatically authorize activating that update
  + failed stopped resumable complete and awaiting-review states remain distinct
  + every new SOP and update preserves causal source work evidence verifier result and unresolved frontier lineage

& [ExistingSubstrateToAudit]
  + SOP query procedure authorship compilation validation coordination runtime and tool surfaces
  + iterative attention stopped terminal-pending checkpoint custody discovery and replay surfaces
  + candidate workspace admission compiler lifecycle verification and provider-free product workflow
  + supervised local service operator bootstrap configuration diagnostics package and signature mechanics
  + shared-attention and nested-host identity contract sequence

& [SourceBoundary]
  + this source preserves the target and authorizes source-to-substrate planning and SJS contract formation
  + it does not by itself authorize workspace mutation commit push self-signature provider execution process launch installation download persistence remote effect FPGA or Minecraft action
  + independent untracked neural-host drafts remain excluded and confer no authority

& [Next]
  + keep NHC-01 outer identity as the first nested-host dependency
  + add a separately governed SOP boot session work-cycle update-broker verification and self-authorship sequence to the product plan
  + require provider-free fixtures before live model-driven self-work
